3.3. CENTRE FOR CONSERVATION EDUCATION.- The following research, training and

educational activities will be taken up by this Centre: -

(1) Develop specific programme and learning resources tailor-made for various stakeholder requirements;

(2)to conduct internship programme, scholar exchange programme, certificate courses, Diploma courses, Under Graduate and Post Graduate Dissertations and Doctoral research etc., in the field of wildlife studies;

(3) Create a database of accredited resources for various programmes, thereby enhancing and ensuring effective outreach;

(4) Develop web-based learning programme for better outreach;

(5) Put to practice a well laid and effective feedback mechanism for constant innovation and improvements;

(6) Coordinate closely with other training institutes and centres established under the Tamil Nadu Forest Department for effective utilization of resources in wildlife conservation outreach programmes; and

(7) to take-up sociological studies including community participation and public perception on conservation.

3.4. CENTRE FOR CONSERVATION ECOLOGY.- The following research works will be taken up by this Centre:-

(1) This centre will focus on restoration of wildlife species and their supporting ecosystems;

(2) Study of marine biodiversity of Gulf of Mannar with special reference to marine mammal conservation;

(3) Study of terrestrial ecosystem of Western Ghats and associated large felines, mega herbivore population and its conservation;

(4) The Centre will focus on adopting a multi-pronged approach that includes research, technology aided management support, training and capacity building of the implementing agencies, monitoring of population and habitats, stakeholder sensitization and mobilization and mitigation of climate threats in priority habitats;

(5) to document and create a database of good practices in wildlife and conservation ecology; and

(6) to create opportunities for institutional networking and collaborative research in the field of wildlife and ecological conservation.

3.5. The Society will review, evaluate and approve establishment of other research and development centres as per the contemporary requirements and relevance from time to time. For example, Centre for Reproductive Biology, Centre for Conservation and Evolutionary Genetics, Centre for Migratory Birds, Centre for Species Survival, Centre for Climate Change and Centre for Emerging Technologies for Wildlife Conservation.

3.6. The Society will also strive to develop and disseminate standards and guidelines pertaining to all the above, wherever applicable.

4, BENEFITS OF THE SOCIETY.- The purpose and objective of the Society stated herein above shall be for the ultimate benefit of the Advanced Institute for Wildlife Conservation, in taking up research studies to aid the survival and recovery of species and their habitats to ensure health and well-being of wildlife in captivity and in wild. As a research institute, the society has to deliver quality multi-disciplinary wildlife research and laboratory outputs within bounded time limit, incurring considerable incidental expenditures for which financial independency of the society is very important.
